Description: FortiGate network identity and Pi-hole DNS policy synchronization
 forti-pihole keeps a FortiGate's devices and networks in step with Pi-hole's
 DNS filtering groups. Devices are classified by MAC into groups kept as
 native FortiOS address groups; each network maps to Pi-hole client entries,
 either as a whole VLAN subnet or as DHCP address slices on a flat network
 (members get reservations inside their group's CIDR slice).
 .
 It is never in the traffic path. A systemd user timer (shipped, never
 enabled) runs it periodically; nothing on the network depends on it running.
 The optional forti-piholed service (a user unit, also never enabled)
 receives FortiGate config-change webhooks and reconciles promptly.
 It writes only address objects and address groups that carry its own name
 prefix and ownership marker, and never touches interfaces, policies,
 routing, DHCP or administrator-created objects.
 .
 It is not VLAN tagging, RADIUS or layer-2 isolation. Device profiles and
 credentials are managed with `forti configure` from the forti-cli package;
 the command engine it shares with forti is compiled in.
